{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-72a3e659-d45a-4036-8054-5d5285db774b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a14accd6477ddc4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8008-he9uvf4f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8008-E004.md","content":"# KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller\n\n## Description\n\nImplement the downstream authentication context for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA\nPrometheus-type triggers on OpenShift. On OpenShift, KEDA ScaledObjects cannot query Thanos/Prometheus\nwithout an authenticated context; this epic adds a parallel reconciler flow in odh-model-controller that\ncreates the per-namespace authentication resources for LLMInferenceServices configured with standalone\nKEDA Prometheus triggers, following the existing pattern used for v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA\nautoscaling (the `kserve_keda_reconciler`).\n\n## Scope\n\n- A reconciler flow in odh-model-controller that detects LLMInferenceService resources configured with\n  standalone KEDA Prometheus-type triggers and creates the per-namespace authentication context:\n  - a dedicated ServiceAccount (`inference-prometheus-auth`),\n  - a ServiceAccountToken Secret (`kubernetes.io/service-account-token` type),\n  - a Role/RoleBinding granting metrics access,\n  - a KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR supplying the bearer token and CA cert to KEDA's Prometheus triggers.\n- Owner reference management and lifecycle cleanup for these resources, following the existing\n  reconciler's approach to resource naming and ownership.\n- No authentication resources created for LLMInferenceServices without standalone KEDA Prometheus\n  triggers (including WVA-path and static deployments).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an LLMInferenceService with standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers, when the controller reconciles,\n  then the ServiceAccount, ServiceAccountToken Secret, Role/RoleBinding, and TriggerAuthentication\n  resources exist in the workload namespace.\n- KEDA Prometheus triggers referencing the TriggerAuthentication successfully execute authenticated\n  queries against Thanos/Prometheus on OpenShift (queries return results over TLS 1.2+ with the\n  ServiceAccount token).\n- Given deletion of the LLMInferenceService (or removal of its standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers),\n  then the owned authentication resources are cleaned up via owner references.\n- Given an LLMInferenceService without standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers, when the controller\n  reconciles, then no authentication resources are created for it.\n- No regression to the existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication flow.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0: standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment) —\n  delivers the OpenShift authentication context that makes Prometheus triggers functional.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45529,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f04e6e5488e1953","agent_id":"a40465497dc7933d4","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"26b0bba3-422e-4cba-b211-43ebc9125421","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:04:07.890Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008 into epics"}
