 OpenShift.\n- KEDA as a documented prerequisite: RHOAI does not auto-install KEDA (platform policy); include\n  installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository (ODH-ADR-0007).\n- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments (KEDA polling load at scale), based on the\n  Performance/PSAP team's input.\n- Scale-from-zero latency expectations reflecting the agreed p50/p95 targets from the llm-d team (the\n  RFE references a 60-second p50 threshold).\n- Troubleshooting section: misconfigured triggers failing the zero-to-one transition, metric outage\n  behavior, and CEL validation errors.\n- Supported configuration matrix for autoscaling paths x deployment topologies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Decision guide, configuration recipes, supported configuration matrix, and troubleshooting topics\n  exist and cover both autoscaling paths and static allocation.\n- Technically reviewed against the implementation by the engineering teams owning the autoscaling paths\n  (API surface, validation behavior, status conditions, TriggerAuthentication flow).\n- Content validated for accuracy against the architecture context (workload-variant-autoscaler, kserve,\n  llm-d, odh-model-controller) — no claims that contradict the architecture record.\n- KEDA prerequisite and installation guidance is included, consistent with the platform policy of not\n  auto-installing external operator dependencies.\n- Recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics and example\n  ScaledObject templates are included.\n- Scale-from-zero latency guidance reflects the agreed p50/p95 targets, and Prometheus capacity guidance\n  for fleet-scale deployments is included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P0: scale-to-zero) — documents configuration and behavior.\n- HLR-4 (P0: scale-from-zero) — documents recommended trigger configurations and cold-start\n  expectations.\n- HLR-5 (P0: disaggregated independent scaling) — documents per-phase recipes.\n- HLR-6 (P1: scaling events visible with signal attribution) — documents operator observability of\n  scaling events on both paths.\n- HLR-7 (P1: well-lit path documentation with decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46229,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f04e6e5488e1953","agent_id":"a40465497dc7933d4","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"cbacf334-a3d0-4e13-8ba6-433b08ef67d3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:04:22.392Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8008 into epics"}
