{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a879fdd6c4feb410","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate downstream adaptation needs for upstream standalone KEDA PR (kserve/kserve#5839)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: INFERENG Midstream\n6\tteam: Serving team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate downstream adaptation needs for upstream standalone KEDA PR (kserve/kserve#5839)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question: does the upstream standalone KEDA\n30\timplementation for LLMInferenceService (kserve/kserve#5839, design kserve/kserve#5646) require\n31\tdownstream adaptation in the RHOAI kserve midstream beyond the odh-model-controller authentication\n32\tcontext? The answer determines the scope and approach of the llmisvc-controller implementation work\n33\t(potential RBAC and TLS adjustments for OpenShift, release-branch integration, backport vs.\n34\tcarry-patch).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Review kserve/kserve#5839 (API types, CEL validation, controller branching, status conditions) against\n39\t  the RHOAI kserve midstream release branch.\n40\t- Enumerate the downstream adaptations required to land standalone KEDA support for LLMInferenceService\n41\t  in the midstream, including any RBAC changes, TLS/OpenShift-specific adjustments, and\n42\t  v1alpha2 API surface deltas that downstream consumers (odh-model-controller) build against.\n43\t- Assess the integration path: backport once the PR merges upstream vs. carrying the patch downstream if\n44\t  the PR is delayed, with a recommendation.\n45\t- Confirm the final `spec.scaling.keda` API shape (pollingInterval, cooldownPeriod, triggers) that\n46\t  downstream consumers and documentation will be written against.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A written assessment listing every required downstream adaptation (or explicitly stating none beyond\n51\t  the authentication context), each traceable to a specific delta between the upstream PR and the\n52\t  midstream codebase.\n53\t- A recommendation with rationale for backport vs. carry-patch integration, including the trigger\n54\t  conditions under which the carry-patch fallback should be invoked.\n55\t- The confirmed standalone KEDA API surface documented so the consumer reconciler and documentation work\n56\t  can proceed against it.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-1 (P0: standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without WVA) — this investigation\n61\t  enables and scopes the implementing work.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf9e7164d9e880b6","agent_id":"a3b6cb1056e7fde20","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"8886c499-d337-48c5-b153-82d595fe5121","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.350Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a879fdd6c4feb410","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
