{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83f017db50cf3eb2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E004\n3\ttitle: KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: INFERENG Midstream\n6\tteam: Serving team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tImplement the downstream authentication context for LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA\n35\tPrometheus-type triggers on OpenShift. On OpenShift, KEDA ScaledObjects cannot query Thanos/Prometheus\n36\twithout an authenticated context; this epic adds a parallel reconciler flow in odh-model-controller that\n37\tcreates the per-namespace authentication resources for LLMInferenceServices configured with standalone\n38\tKEDA Prometheus triggers, following the existing pattern used for v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA\n39\tautoscaling (the `kserve_keda_reconciler`).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A reconciler flow in odh-model-controller that detects LLMInferenceService resources configured with\n44\t  standalone KEDA Prometheus-type triggers and creates the per-namespace authentication context:\n45\t  - a dedicated ServiceAccount (`inference-prometheus-auth`),\n46\t  - a ServiceAccountToken Secret (`kubernetes.io/service-account-token` type),\n47\t  - a Role/RoleBinding granting metrics access,\n48\t  - a KEDA TriggerAuthentication CR supplying the bearer token and CA cert to KEDA's Prometheus triggers.\n49\t- Owner reference management and lifecycle cleanup for these resources, following the existing\n50\t  reconciler's approach to resource naming and ownership.\n51\t- No authentication resources created for LLMInferenceServices without standalone KEDA Prometheus\n52\t  triggers (including WVA-path and static deployments).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers, when the controller reconciles,\n57\t  then the ServiceAccount, ServiceAccountToken Secret, Role/RoleBinding, and TriggerAuthentication\n58\t  resources exist in the workload namespace.\n59\t- KEDA Prometheus triggers referencing the TriggerAuthentication successfully execute authenticated\n60\t  queries against Thanos/Prometheus on OpenShift (queries return results over TLS 1.2+ with the\n61\t  ServiceAccount token).\n62\t- Given deletion of the LLMInferenceService (or removal of its standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers),\n63\t  then the owned authentication resources are cleaned up via owner references.\n64\t- Given an LLMInferenceService without standalone KEDA Prometheus triggers, when the controller\n65\t  reconciles, then no authentication resources are created for it.\n66\t- No regression to the existing v1beta1 InferenceService KEDA authentication flow.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0: standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment) —\n71\t  delivers the OpenShift authentication context that makes Prometheus triggers functional.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf9e7164d9e880b6","agent_id":"a3b6cb1056e7fde20","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"30a26c43-3ede-401c-88b1-6c48ae1bfcef","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:06:59.035Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83f017db50cf3eb2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
