{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c645aa1d7a3b844","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8008 (Inference-Aware Autoscaling for llm-d: KEDA primitives)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: neither below-threshold nor docs-only. The strategy is M-effort (2-3 sprints), spans multiple\n13\tcomponents (KServe llmisvc-controller, odh-model-controller, Documentation), multiple teams (Serving,\n14\tDocumentation), and multiple architecturally distinct work streams (two Go controller codebases plus\n15\tsubstantive docs authoring). It also contains genuine unknowns flagged as \"needs validation\" assumptions\n16\tand open questions. Full decomposition follows.\n17\t\n18\tStaff Engineer Input: present but empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to log.\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E001 | Investigate downstream adaptation needs for upstream standalone KEDA PR (kserve/kserve#5839) | Investigation | Serving team | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E002 | Validate KEDA scale-to/from-zero behavior and EPP metrics availability at zero replicas | Investigation | Serving team | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E003 | Standalone KEDA autoscaling path in KServe llmisvc-controller | Implementation | Serving team | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E004 | KEDA TriggerAuthentication reconciler for LLMInferenceService in odh-model-controller | Implementation | Serving team | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8008-E005 | Autoscaling documentation: decision guide, configuration recipes, troubleshooting | Implementation | Documentation team | P0 (docs-authoring exception: strategy priority Critical → P0) |\n29\t\n30\t## Dependency DAG\n31\t\n32\t```mermaid\n33\tgraph TD\n34\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8008-E001 Investigation: downstream adaptation assessment] --> E003\n35\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8008-E002 Investigation: scale-to/from-zero validation] --> E003\n36\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8008-E003 Implementation: llmisvc-controller standalone KEDA] --> E004\n37\t    E003 --> E005\n38\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-8008-E004 Implementation: TriggerAuthentication reconciler] --> E005\n39\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-8008-E005 Implementation: docs-authoring]\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tE001 and E002 start immediately and in parallel (both are answerable without the standalone KEDA\n43\timplementation: E001 is a public-PR/repo desk assessment; E002 can exercise KEDA ScaledObjects and EPP\n44\tmetrics against existing deployments).\n45\t\n46\t## DAG Justification\n47\t\n48\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n49\t|------|------|-----------|\n50\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates Implementation) | The open question \"does kserve/kserve#5839 require downstream adaptation beyond authentication context?\" determines the scope/approach of the llmisvc-controller work (RBAC, TLS, OpenShift adjustments, backport vs carry-patch). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n51\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates Implementation) | Two strategy assumptions are flagged \"needs validation\": KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` pause/resume correctness for LLM workloads, and EPP flow-control queue metrics availability at zero replicas. Both underpin the P0 scale-to-zero/scale-from-zero HLRs delivered by this implementation. True gate: `add_remediation` (a failed validation adds remediation work rather than removing the epic). Combined into one Investigation because a single scale-to/from-zero validation exercise produces both answers and one deliverable. |\n52\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 13 (API producer → consumer serial) | The odh-model-controller reconciler builds against the new `spec.scaling.keda` API surface (standalone KEDA spec, trigger fields) produced by the llmisvc-controller work; the CRD field must exist before the consumer reconciler can detect and act on it. |\n53\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation describes what was built; it must reflect the final API surface, validation behavior, and status conditions. |\n54\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | The docs must document the TriggerAuthentication flow for OpenShift Prometheus triggers that this reconciler delivers. |\n55\t\n56\tNotable non-edges:\n57\t\n58\t- No edge from E002 to E004: the TriggerAuthentication reconciler follows the existing v1beta1\n59\t  `kserve_keda_reconciler` pattern and does not depend on scale-to/from-zero behavior.\n60\t- No edge from E001/E002 to E005 directly: transitively covered via E003.\n61\t- No konflux-onboarding / repo-onboarding / license-validation epics: kserve and odh-model-controller\n62\t  are existing in-platform components (architecture context files exist for both), and no new repo or\n63\t  image is introduced.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n66\t\n67\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n68\t|-----|----------|-------|\n69\t| HLR-1: Standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without WVA | P0 | E003 (implements), E004 (OpenShift auth context), E001 (enables) |\n70\t| HLR-2: Mutual exclusivity of WVA and standalone KEDA paths (CEL, at-least-one/at-most-one) | P0 | E003 |\n71\t| HLR-3: Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths) | P0 | E002 (validates), E003 (implements), E005 (documents) |\n72\t| HLR-4: Scale-from-zero (WVA via EPP queue metrics; standalone KEDA via user triggers) | P0 | E002 (validates), E003 (implements), E005 (documents trigger configurations) |\n73\t| HLR-5: Disaggregated prefill/decode pools scale independently | P0 | E003 (phase-specific scaling resources and validation), E005 (recipes) |\n74\t| HLR-6: Scaling events visible with signal attribution | P1 | E003 (scaling status conditions; KEDA ScaledObject events on the standalone path), E005 (operator guidance) |\n75\t| HLR-7: Well-lit path documentation with decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting | P1 | E005 |\n76\t\n77\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority-split check (Step 4): E003 spans P0 HLRs and\n78\tthe P1 observability HLR, but scaling status conditions share the same controller surfaces and data\n79\tstructures as the scaling path itself — the P1 work is tightly coupled to the same implementation\n80\tsurface, so it stays bundled rather than split.\n81\t\n82\t## Health Warnings\n83\t\n84\t- **Pending human process gates**: Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, License Validation, and other\n85\t  prerequisites are all \"Pending human review\" in the strategy. All Implementation epics are implicitly\n86\t  gated on these strategy-level approvals; this is not modeled as DAG edges.\n87\t- **Metric-outage AC may be a scope trap**: strategy AC 6 (\"Prometheus metrics unavailable → deployment\n88\t  holds its current replica count\") assumes KEDA fallback behavior; KEDA's default on scaler errors may\n89\t  differ unless fallback is configured. The implementing team should confirm KEDA fallback semantics —\n90\t  captured as an acceptance criterion on E003 rather than a new epic (implementation proceeds the same\n91\t  way; failure = fix-and-retry).\n92\t- **Unresolved doc inputs**: the p50/p95 scale-from-zero latency target (owner: llm-d team) and the\n93\t  Prometheus fleet-scale capacity guidance (owner: Performance/PSAP team) are content inputs to the docs\n94\t  epic, not structural unknowns — no epic's existence or approach changes based on their answers. They\n95\t  are captured as acceptance criteria / input requirements on E005. If the targets arrive late, only doc\n96\t  content changes.\n97\t- **Docs epic at P0**: driven by the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority Critical → P0),\n98\t  not by relative urgency; the docs epic is still last in the DAG.\n99\t\n100\t## Tiered Delivery\n101\t\n102\tEvaluated for the external dependency with uncertain timing — upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839 (in\n103\tprogress). Partial value is possible without it, and a viable fallback exists (carry the patch\n104\tdownstream in the midstream kserve repo, backport once merged — per the strategy's own risk mitigation).\n105\tPer Rule 21, the fallback is noted as an acceptance criterion on E003 rather than a separate upstream\n106\tepic, so no hard Tier 1/Tier 2 split is required. Both Investigations (E001, E002) deliver risk-reduction\n107\tvalue immediately and are independent of upstream timing; the Implementation chain (E003 → E004) proceeds\n108\tvia the fallback if the upstream PR is delayed.\n109\t\n110\t## Component Mapping Notes\n111\t\n112\tCanonical RHAI component names (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) do not include \"KServe\" or\n113\t\"odh-model-controller\" as such. Mappings used:\n114\t\n115\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n116\t|----|----|----|\n117\t| KServe (llmisvc-controller) | INFERENG Midstream | Closest parent-level component for kserve midstream (opendatahub-io/red-hat-data-services kserve) controller work |\n118\t| odh-model-controller | INFERENG Midstream | Same midstream inference-engineering component; separate epic because it is a different repo and logical change (Rule 1/14) |\n119\t| EPP flow control metrics / KEDA behavior validation | llm-d | EPP is part of llm-d; validation exercise targets llm-d workload metrics |\n120\t| Documentation | Documentation | Direct match |\n121\t\n122\t## Investigation Scoping Notes\n123\t\n124\t- Open question \"does kserve/kserve#5839 require downstream adaptation beyond authentication context?\"\n125\t  → E001 (answer changes the scope/approach of E003 → Investigation).\n126\t- Assumptions \"KEDA idleReplicaCount correctly pauses/resumes for LLM workloads\" and \"EPP flow control\n127\t  queue metrics reliably available at zero replicas\" (both \"needs validation\") → E002 (answers change\n128\t  what E003/E005 must do; combined — one validation exercise, one deliverable).\n129\t- Open question \"target p50/p95 for scale-from-zero time\" → not an Investigation; determines docs\n130\t  recommendations only (content input to E005, captured as AC).\n131\t- Open question \"Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale\" → not an Investigation; doc content input\n132\t  to E005, captured as AC.\n133\t- Remaining assumption (\"v1alpha2 spec.scaling fields stable\" — confirmed via overlay 0011; \"v1beta1 KEDA\n134\t  reconciler as reference\" — confirmed via architecture context) requires no epic.\n135\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a378c0c54cb7b","agent_id":"afa7e05e1e481405b","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"2ac963a6-bde4-4c6f-b662-df8f85265c89","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:09.305Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c645aa1d7a3b844","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
