{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a74ddda2a8af2d4c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n3\ttitle: Validate KEDA scale-to/from-zero behavior and EPP metrics availability at zero\n4\t  replicas\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n6\tcomponent: llm-d\n7\tteam: Serving team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate KEDA scale-to/from-zero behavior and EPP metrics availability at zero replicas\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation validates two assumptions the strategy explicitly flags as \"needs validation\", both\n31\tof which underpin the P0 scale-to-zero and scale-from-zero requirements for the standalone KEDA\n32\tautoscaling path:\n33\t\n34\t1. A KEDA ScaledObject with `idleReplicaCount: 0` correctly pauses and resumes scaling for LLM inference\n35\t   workloads (scale to zero on idle, scale back up when the trigger fires).\n36\t2. EPP flow control queue metrics are reliably exposed when inference pods are at zero replicas (the EPP\n37\t   itself remains running), so user-configured standalone KEDA triggers can drive the zero-to-one\n38\t   transition.\n39\t\n40\tThe validation can be performed against existing deployments with manually constructed ScaledObjects —\n41\tit does not require the LLMInferenceService standalone KEDA controller path to exist first.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Exercise KEDA scale-to-zero (`idleReplicaCount: 0`, cooldown period) against an LLM inference\n46\t  deployment; confirm replica count reaches 0, the ScaledObject reports idle, and capacity is released.\n47\t- Exercise scale-from-zero via a Prometheus trigger on EPP flow control queue metrics; confirm the\n48\t  zero-to-one transition occurs when a request is queued for an idle model, and measure trigger-to-serving\n49\t  latency characteristics.\n50\t- Confirm EPP flow control queue size and dispatch rate metrics remain scrapeable while inference pods\n51\t  are at zero replicas.\n52\t- Capture recommended trigger configurations for scale-from-zero using EPP queue metrics and example\n53\t  ScaledObject templates (these feed the operator documentation).\n54\t- Record any KEDA fallback behavior observed when Prometheus metrics become unavailable (does the\n55\t  deployment hold its current replica count?), to inform the implementation's acceptance criteria.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Pass/fail result for each of the two validated assumptions, with evidence (metrics, ScaledObject\n60\t  status, replica timelines).\n61\t- Recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations and example ScaledObject templates using EPP flow\n62\t  control queue metrics, ready for inclusion in operator documentation.\n63\t- If either assumption fails, a documented description of the failure mode and candidate remediation\n64\t  options for the implementing team.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P0: scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0`) — validates the mechanism.\n69\t- HLR-4 (P0: scale-from-zero; standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers) — validates the trigger\n70\t  approach and produces the recommended configurations.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a378c0c54cb7b","agent_id":"afa7e05e1e481405b","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"3fbdada0-8386-4c5c-b2be-e2a0678a8b1e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:13.105Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a74ddda2a8af2d4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
