{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f80ae1b2e27b33","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n3\ttitle: Standalone KEDA autoscaling path in KServe llmisvc-controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: INFERENG Midstream\n6\tteam: Serving team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8008-E001,RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream adaptation assessment reveals substantial downstream\n16\t    changes (RBAC, TLS, OpenShift adjustments) beyond backporting kserve/kserve#5839,\n17\t    rewrite this epic's scope around the required adaptations; if the scale-to/from-zero\n18\t    validation fails, add remediation work for the scale-to-zero/scale-from-zero approach;\n19\t    if the upstream PR is delayed, carry the patch downstream in the midstream repo\n20\t    and backport once merged.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: -1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 3\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Standalone KEDA autoscaling path in KServe llmisvc-controller\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tImplement standalone KEDA autoscaling as a first-class path for LLMInferenceService, alongside the\n43\texisting WVA-mediated path, following the upstream design in kserve/kserve#5646 and implementation in\n44\tkserve/kserve#5839. Users configure KEDA triggers directly in the LLMInferenceService spec without\n45\tdeploying WVA. This epic delivers the API types, CEL validation, controller branching, and scaling\n46\tstatus conditions in the llmisvc-controller, and integrates the upstream standalone KEDA support into\n47\tthe RHOAI kserve midstream.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Integrate kserve/kserve#5839 into the RHOAI kserve midstream release branch (backport once merged\n52\t  upstream, or carry the patch downstream if the upstream PR is delayed), including any downstream\n53\t  adaptations identified by the upstream adaptation assessment (potential RBAC and TLS/OpenShift\n54\t  adjustments).\n55\t- API type changes in the v1alpha2 LLMInferenceService ScalingSpec: standalone KEDA configuration with\n56\t  `pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`, and user-defined `triggers` (type, metadata map).\n57\t- CEL validation changes: relax the rule requiring `wva` to require at least one of `wva` or `keda`,\n58\t  enforce at-most-one (mutual exclusivity), validate trigger completeness, and enforce that\n59\t  disaggregated deployments use the same scaling path for prefill and decode phases (actuator\n60\t  consistency per overlay 0011).\n61\t- Scaling controller branching: when standalone KEDA is configured, create a ScaledObject with the\n62\t  user-provided triggers (including `idleReplicaCount: 0` for scale-to-zero) and skip VariantAutoscaling\n63\t  CR creation entirely; the WVA path is unchanged.\n64\t- Phase-specific scaling resources for disaggregated prefill and decode pools so each scales\n65\t  independently based on its load profile.\n66\t- Scaling status conditions covering both paths so operators can observe scaling state and signal\n67\t  attribution (KEDA ScaledObject events for the standalone path; WVA events for the WVA path).\n68\t- Maintain backwards compatibility: existing CRs with `spec.scaling.wva` continue to work unchanged, and\n69\t  static deployments with no `spec.scaling` produce no scaling resources.\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with standalone KEDA configured with user-defined triggers and no WVA\n74\t  deployed, when the trigger condition is met (e.g., a Prometheus query threshold exceeded), then the\n75\t  deployment scales up — measured by KEDA ScaledObject status showing active and Deployment replica count\n76\t  increasing.\n77\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with both `spec.scaling.wva` and `spec.scaling.keda` set, when the CR is\n78\t  submitted, then the API server rejects it with a CEL validation error indicating mutual exclusivity.\n79\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with standalone KEDA and no WVA, when the controller reconciles, then no\n80\t  VariantAutoscaling CR is created and a ScaledObject with the user-provided triggers is created —\n81\t  measured by `kubectl get variantautoscalings` returning empty and `kubectl get scaledobjects` returning\n82\t  a ScaledObject with the user's triggers.\n83\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with KEDA and `idleReplicaCount: 0`, when no requests are received for\n84\t  the cooldown period, then the deployment scales to zero — measured by Deployment replica count\n85\t  reaching 0 and KEDA ScaledObject status showing idle.\n86\t- Given a disaggregated LLMInferenceService with separate scaling configs, when prefill pods reach\n87\t  saturation while decode pods remain below threshold, then only the prefill pool scales up — measured by\n88\t  independent scaling resource status for prefill and decode roles.\n89\t- Given a deployment with autoscaling active, when Prometheus metrics become unavailable, then the\n90\t  deployment holds its current replica count — measured by replica count remaining stable during the\n91\t  metric outage (confirm KEDA fallback semantics; configure fallback if the default does not hold).\n92\t- Static deployments with no autoscaling configured continue to serve identically — measured by no\n93\t  VariantAutoscaling, HPA, or ScaledObject resources created for deployments without `spec.scaling`.\n94\t- Existing LLMInferenceService CRs with `spec.scaling.wva` behave identically before and after this\n95\t  change (additive path, no regression).\n96\t- If upstream kserve/kserve#5839 has not merged when this work is scheduled, the patch is carried\n97\t  downstream in the midstream repo and backported once merged upstream (fallback per strategy risk\n98\t  mitigation).\n99\t\n100\t## HLR Traceability\n101\t\n102\t- HLR-1 (P0: standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without requiring WVA deployment)\n103\t- HLR-2 (P0: mutual exclusivity of the two autoscaling paths at the API level with CEL validation)\n104\t- HLR-3 (P0: scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0`)\n105\t- HLR-4 (P0: scale-from-zero via user-configured triggers on the standalone path)\n106\t- HLR-5 (P0: disaggregated prefill and decode pools scale independently)\n107\t- HLR-6 (P1: scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution)\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a378c0c54cb7b","agent_id":"afa7e05e1e481405b","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"c2c726e3-5a33-4816-9024-ab9f809add27","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:17.294Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f80ae1b2e27b33","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
