{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d61576c759a7fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E005\n3\ttitle: 'Autoscaling documentation: decision guide, configuration recipes, troubleshooting'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E004\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Autoscaling documentation: decision guide, configuration recipes, troubleshooting\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAuthor the operator-facing documentation for LLMInferenceService autoscaling, covering both autoscaling\n36\tpaths (WVA-mediated and standalone KEDA) and static allocation. This is the well-lit path required by\n37\tthe strategy: a decision guide for choosing between the paths, configuration recipes per workload shape,\n38\ta supported configuration matrix, and troubleshooting guidance.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Decision guide comparing WVA-mediated autoscaling, standalone KEDA, and static allocation, with\n43\t  use-case-based recommendations (e.g., inference-aware WVA signals vs. simpler trigger-based scaling;\n44\t  the business-hours coding-assistant scenario).\n45\t- Configuration reference for the standalone KEDA path: the ScalingSpec standalone KEDA fields\n46\t  (pollingInterval, cooldownPeriod, triggers), mutual exclusivity with the WVA path and with static\n47\t  replicas, and CEL validation error meanings.\n48\t- Configuration recipes per workload shape, including disaggregated prefill/decode deployments with\n49\t  independent per-phase scaling and scale-to-zero/scale-from-zero configurations.\n50\t- Recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics, with example\n51\t  ScaledObject templates, and realistic cold-start time expectations (referencing the model\n52\t  startup/fast-load initiatives; recommend headroom configuration for latency-sensitive workloads).\n53\t- Instructions for operators to reference the TriggerAuthentication resource in KEDA trigger definitions\n54\t  for authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n55\t- KEDA as a documented prerequisite: RHOAI does not auto-install KEDA (platform policy); include\n56\t  installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository (ODH-ADR-0007).\n57\t- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments (KEDA polling load at scale), based on the\n58\t  Performance/PSAP team's input.\n59\t- Scale-from-zero latency expectations reflecting the agreed p50/p95 targets from the llm-d team (the\n60\t  RFE references a 60-second p50 threshold).\n61\t- Troubleshooting section: misconfigured triggers failing the zero-to-one transition, metric outage\n62\t  behavior, and CEL validation errors.\n63\t- Supported configuration matrix for autoscaling paths x deployment topologies.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Decision guide, configuration recipes, supported configuration matrix, and troubleshooting topics\n68\t  exist and cover both autoscaling paths and static allocation.\n69\t- Technically reviewed against the implementation by the engineering teams owning the autoscaling paths\n70\t  (API surface, validation behavior, status conditions, TriggerAuthentication flow).\n71\t- Content validated for accuracy against the architecture context (workload-variant-autoscaler, kserve,\n72\t  llm-d, odh-model-controller) — no claims that contradict the architecture record.\n73\t- KEDA prerequisite and installation guidance is included, consistent with the platform policy of not\n74\t  auto-installing external operator dependencies.\n75\t- Recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics and example\n76\t  ScaledObject templates are included.\n77\t- Scale-from-zero latency guidance reflects the agreed p50/p95 targets, and Prometheus capacity guidance\n78\t  for fleet-scale deployments is included.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-3 (P0: scale-to-zero) — documents configuration and behavior.\n83\t- HLR-4 (P0: scale-from-zero) — documents recommended trigger configurations and cold-start\n84\t  expectations.\n85\t- HLR-5 (P0: disaggregated independent scaling) — documents per-phase recipes.\n86\t- HLR-6 (P1: scaling events visible with signal attribution) — documents operator observability of\n87\t  scaling events on both paths.\n88\t- HLR-7 (P1: well-lit path documentation with decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting)\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a378c0c54cb7b","agent_id":"afa7e05e1e481405b","session_id":"a7d955e8-9b81-49a1-9fe3-77d8218dfc96","uuid":"63c735fe-ae45-40d2-9c06-4ff2cdd60a74","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:13:18.828Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d61576c759a7fd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
